---@alias gcp.accesscontextmanager_v1.ServicePerimeterPerimeterTypeEnum "PERIMETER_TYPE_REGULAR"|"PERIMETER_TYPE_BRIDGE"

---Stores settings related to Google Cloud Session Length, including session duration, the type of challenge (that is, method) a user faces when their session expires, and other related settings.
---@class gcp.accesscontextmanager_v1.SessionSettings
---@field sessionReauthMethod? gcp.accesscontextmanager_v1.SessionSettingsSessionReauthMethodEnum|string Optional. Session challenge method when a user's Google Cloud session expires.
---@field maxInactivity? string Optional. How long a user is allowed to take between actions before a new access token must be issued. Only set for Google Cloud apps.
---@field useOidcMaxAge? boolean Optional. Only useful for OIDC apps. When `false`, the OIDC `max_age` parameter, if passed in the authentication request, is ignored. When `true`, the re-authentication period is the minimum of the `session_length` field and the `max_age` OIDC parameter.
---@field sessionLength? string Optional. The session length. Setting this field to zero allows for sessions that are active indefinitely. Also, setting `session_length_enabled` to `false` disregards session limits, which means that sessions never expire. If `use_oidc_max_age` is `true`, for OIDC apps, the session length will be the minimum of this field and the OIDC `max_age` parameter. If this field is set to zero, `session_length_enabled` must be set to `false` or left unset.
---@field sessionLengthEnabled? boolean Optional. This field enables or disables Google Cloud session length. When `false`, all fields set above are disregarded and the session length is effectively infinite. If `session_length` is set to zero, this field must be set to `false`.

---@alias gcp.accesscontextmanager_v1.SessionSettingsSessionReauthMethodEnum "SESSION_REAUTH_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOGIN"|"SECURITY_KEY"|"PASSWORD"

